      {
        "id": 233921,
        "name": "Under3",
        "username": "Under3",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/under3/{size}/1872_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-10-17T23:50:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There is no rule that \"a bonus can only apply to one effect per action.\" I think you might be confusing it with a bonus can only be applied to one effect die.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>An effect die is a specific term though rather than each individual effect - it's the die that is used to do the effect(s). If you have a mod and a die gets modified everything that die does is modified. For example if you attack multiple targets with your mid die, and you have a mod of +3 applied to your mid die every target hit take the hit with that +3. I see no reason why the mod wouldn't apply to both effects here too.</p>\n<p>The rule that a mod can only apply to one effect die means if there's multiple effect die in a roll (such as attack with mid and hinder with min) you choose just one of those for the mod to apply to, which isn't the case in this example - in this situation there is only one effect die.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:09:52.526Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 20315,
        "topic_slug": "bonuses-with-untouchable-empowerment-question",
        "display_username": "Under3",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>There is no rule that \"a bonus can only apply to one effect per action.\" I think you might be confusing it with a bonus can only be applied to one effect die.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>An effect die is a specific term though rather than each individual effect - it's the die that is used to do the effect(s). If you have a mod and a die gets modified everything that die does is modified. For example if you attack multiple targets with your mid die, and you have a mod of +3 applied to your mid die every target hit take the hit with that +3. I see no reason why the mod wouldn't apply to both effects here too.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The rule that a mod can only apply to one effect die means if there's multiple effect die in a roll (such as attack with mid and hinder with min) you choose just one of those for the mod to apply to, which isn't the case in this example - in this situation there is only one effect die.</p>",
